From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:20:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 191/194] hjviewer: review fixes for the wait on a refused
 connection window's pipe

What could happen: when the --server found the connection window's pipe
there but refused (src/server/connection.rs start_ipc, name_taken), it
still started a window at once. That window cannot take the name
(parity-tokio-ipc makes the first instance) and quits, so every incoming
connection during the wait started a doomed GUI process in the user's
session. And the 40 tries were not renewed when the name came free: if the
refused window closed late, the window started then could get under a
second to reach new_listener, and the connection failed anyway.

What changes (Windows only, name_taken is never set elsewhere): with the
name taken, no window is started until a try finds the pipe missing
(ipc::is_endpoint_missing); then one is started and gets the usual 20 tries
(6 s) from that moment. The first refusal is logged once per connection,
and a wait that ends with the name still taken says so.

Left alone: a missing pipe at the start, and Linux and macOS, behave as
before (start the window, 20 tries).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/server/connection.rs | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/server/connection.rs b/src/server/connection.rs
index 8facdca..1a2aa90 100644
--- a/src/server/connection.rs
+++ b/src/server/connection.rs
@@ -6467,22 +6467,35 @@ async fn start_ipc(
         sleep(1.).await;
     }
     let mut stream = None;
-    // Windows: the name is this session's (ipc::cm_postfix), so a window left open in another
+    // The name is this session's on Windows (ipc::cm_postfix), so a window left open in another
     // session does not hold it. A pipe of that name that is there but refuses this process
     // (src/ipc/windows.rs: another copy of the app, or another account that took the name) keeps
-    // it, so the window started below cannot serve it and ends at once. Such a window closes
-    // itself about 6 s after its last connection; wait longer then, and start ours again once
-    // the name is free.
+    // it, and a window started now could not serve it and would end at once. Such a window
+    // closes itself about 6 s after its last connection: wait longer then, without starting
+    // one, and start ours once the name is free, with the usual time to come up.
     let cm_postfix = crate::ipc::cm_postfix();
     let mut name_taken = false;
     match crate::ipc::connect(1000, &cm_postfix).await {
         Ok(s) => stream = Some(s),
-        Err(err) => name_taken = cfg!(windows) && !crate::ipc::is_endpoint_missing(&err),
+        Err(err) => {
+            name_taken = cfg!(windows) && !crate::ipc::is_endpoint_missing(&err);
+            if name_taken {
+                log::warn!(
+                    "The connection window's pipe is held by an untrusted process, wait: {err}"
+                );
+            }
+        }
     }
     if stream.is_none() {
-        start_cm_process().await?;
-        let tries = if name_taken { 40 } else { 20 };
-        for _ in 0..tries {
+        const CM_START_TRIES: u32 = 20;
+        let mut tries = if name_taken {
+            40
+        } else {
+            start_cm_process().await?;
+            CM_START_TRIES
+        };
+        while tries > 0 {
+            tries -= 1;
             sleep(0.3).await;
             match crate::ipc::connect(1000, &cm_postfix).await {
                 Ok(s) => {
@@ -6493,10 +6506,14 @@ async fn start_ipc(
                     name_taken = false;
                     log::info!("The connection window's pipe is free again, start cm");
                     start_cm_process().await?;
+                    tries = CM_START_TRIES;
                 }
                 Err(_) => {}
             }
         }
+        if stream.is_none() && name_taken {
+            log::warn!("The connection window's pipe was not freed, give up");
+        }
     }
     if stream.is_none() {
         bail!("Failed to connect to connection manager");
